I never saw my friend again and this is  that story so it was many years ago and  I was walking my dog and Brooklyn one  night little tiny white Jack Russell  Chihuahua it was very very hot and I  just wanted to go home and I was saying  make poopie make poopie I have no  empirical evidence that this creates  poop but it was what I was doing and  he'd finally proved we were gonna go  back home and if you've ever lived in  New York this summer can be very sultry  and disgusting and I just wanted to get  inside when I see this guy walking  towards us down the street with a little  dog our leash my little dog Charlie gets  very excited like wagging getting down  on the ground the other dogs excited now  I have to talk to this total and  complete stranger about nonsense because  we have two animals at the ends of ropes  that want to send each others butts we  start talking just sort of talking about  the weather and he says oh I was just in  Texas I was like oh I'm from Texas  there's like Oh what part I was like San  Antonio was like I was right neither we  had so much great Mexican food oh I miss  the Mexican food don't you love the  guacamole yeah I love the guacamole they  don't know how to do guacamole here am i  right we're just like going back and  forth it's been like half an hour our  dogs are just sort of like chillin next  to each other like checking out the  block at one point I finally tell him  I'm like hey I live right here why don't  we hang out sometime and he says oh well  there's like a weird pause like I don't  know why he's not saying yes let's do  that he's like well I'm um I'm moving  away soon I said oh oh that's fantastic  where are you going and he says I'm  moving to Belize and I'm like oh my god  you're making your American dream come  true of leaving America good for you and  he says yeah I've been going there scuba  diving for years I love it I'm just  gonna like go there and just float in  the ocean and I'm like that  is amazing earlier he had mentioned that  he lived with his dog and his girlfriend  I was like oh are they gonna go with you  to Belize and he got real quiet again  like I said something really wrong and  he says oh they're not coming with me  I'm kinda like mmm okay this is weird  it's real quiet and then he just blurts  out I have terminal cancer and I only  have six months to live  and I kind of don't like know how to  respond and he can see me  flustered and he immediately starts kind  of like spinning out like he starts  apologizing he explains to me that you  know he's been having to tell family  members and friends this information for  months and people have cried and  screamed and he feels like over and over  again he has to comfort them and he said  it was so nice in this moment to tell  you a total stranger and be ok about it  but he starts to apologize and he's kind  of getting tears in his eyes about it  and I want to calm him down  so finally I just blurt it's ok I'm a  storyteller at which point like the  ghost of myself exits the front of my  body walks around it kicks my own ass  like he just basically confronted me  with his mortality and I was like I have  a hobby  and then I freaked out oh my god I mean  I'm so sorry that you're dying me not  that you're dying me hey hey hey no no  it's ok telling you this my experience  my story what I'm going through was  really wonderful to say this to a  stranger and I honestly think the world  would probably be a much better place if  everyone told each other their stories I  said yeah I agree he stood there for a  minute made some small talk and then he  finally said well I've got to go I said  okay well take care and he open his arms  and he hugged me and then I said goodbye  like goodbye you know returned Hren we  walked opposite directions and literally  I probably wasn't ten seconds away from  him when I burst into tears like and I  remember my little dog being like what  you cuz animals they don't get immense  like sobbing or like what's happening do  you want to play I get upstairs in my  apartment and my boyfriend is there and  he was like Davey what happened and I'm  like well I looked at this guy so we  started talking he's gonna die of cancer  and he's like calm down the next day I  woke up and I couldn't stop thinking  about him I did what you do in you know  the 2000s when you meet someone with a  terminal disease I befriended him on  Facebook and they sent him a little  message I just said hey it was nice  meeting you  and over the next six months I watched  his Facebook page and I literally saw  his experience in Belize just through  images  changed his profile pic and his banner  pic I saw beautiful trees swaying on the  beach I saw these sort of underwater  pictures of this beautiful like Azura  ocean I saw like stingrays starfish and  after about six months the pictures just  stopped updating and I knew what had  more than likely happened as it Kevin  had had passed away now during this time  I had actually been really sick too I  had Crohn's disease and I got down to  like a hundred and seventeen pounds I  had been in a bad place but my life  started to change I was feeling  healthier and I was really really  hitting story-telling heart and I  started teaching storytelling I would  use the story of meeting Kevin as a way  to tell students or people I was  coaching or directing about the  importance of sharing their stories you  know people would be working on stories  about domestic abuse or really personal  loss when they would doubt it I would  often time to share this anecdote about  Kevin it was probably about two  two-and-a-half years after I'd met Kevin  when one day I was on Facebook and you  know Facebook had just didn't that thing  where they redesigned the interface and  it made you feel like a senior citizen  like where am I almost dudes like  banging and stuff and I finally found  this thing I didn't know was there it  was like a sub trash folder under a like  span kevin had sent me a message the  night that we met and all it said was it  was so nice talking to you I'd love to  continue this friendship  here's my number  and I immediately burst into tears I'm  so angry I was so frustrated thinking  how did I like miss this chance to  maintain this friendship and I put  Charlie on a leash and I went for a walk  I was probably halfway down the block  when I saw a neighbor of ours and she  could tell I was upset and she's like  what's wrong and I was like well you  know about two 20 years ago I met this  guy on the street with cancer and some  telling her the story  her face shifts and she says oh are you  talking about Kevin that jerk she tells  me the story of Kevin a man who had  subletted her apartment with his  girlfriend and their dog a couple years  earlier him and his girlfriend were  going to part ways he was gonna go to  police he was gonna get her kind of  settled and that she was gonna go and  move west kevin was gonna put her stuff  in storage anyway he went to police and  when she came to the storage unit and  the apartment it was all empty because  Kevin had sold all of her stuff to feed  his crystal meth addiction Kevin did not  have terminal cancer he was a drug  addict I don't know how he developed  this lie I did find out that I was one  of many people in the neighborhood who  had met Kevin one night and held him  while he cried and they cried maybe he  was so caught up in his addiction and  the lies around it and the money he owed  people and the jobs he lost maybe one  night he just tried it out you know he  just wanted to see what does it like to  say I'm dying someone held him and  hugged him and it felt good and I come  away from this conversation and I'm so  angry and I go upstairs back to the  computer and I sit down and I look and  Kevin has sent me a message on Facebook  and it just said hey what's up I click  on Kevin's profile  Kevin moved back to New York he's a  foodie there's pictures of him like  eating chocolate cheesecake hashtag  yummy I am just like in a rage like the  sadness that I had felt down on the  street talking to this woman became this  kind of like like as I look at this like  who the hell does this guy think he is  but then the thing that really hits me  is like not so much that he betrayed me  but I told the story of him too  people who I was teaching and when I  think about having used this story to do  that I'm just like and I spread this  like figurative cancer ironically do you  know what I mean like I used the story  of this dude to impart the importance of  truth to people and it was just a  flat-out lie it made me think about the  importance of stories and why we tell  them I think meeting Kevin served a  purpose in my life and even though the  story that Kevin told me was a lie  the way that it made me feel wasn't  [Music]
 

